ce_uri": "https://www.courtlistener.com/api/rest/v4/docket-entries/439630208/", "id": 439630208, "docket": "https://www.courtlistener.com/api/rest/v4/dockets/71505605/", "recap_documents": [{"resource_uri": "https://www.courtlistener.com/api/rest/v4/recap-documents/454163478/", "id": 454163478, "tags": [], "absolute_url": "/docket/71505605/4/orozco-v-tesla-inc/", "date_created": "2025-10-01T15:37:22.753429-07:00", "date_modified": "2025-11-29T03:40:34.979107-08:00", "sha1": "099bcf2787efe80647f76edef626ccf99f99be9c", "page_count": 3, "file_size": 168201, "filepath_local": "recap/gov.uscourts.cand.457185/gov.uscourts.cand.457185.4.0.pdf", "filepath_ia": "https://archive.org/download/gov.uscourts.cand.457185/gov.uscourts.cand.457185.4.0.pdf", "ia_upload_failure_count": null, "thumbnail": null, "thumbnail_status": 0, "plain_text": "        Case 3:25-cv-08325-PHK           Document 4        Filed 10/01/25      Page 1 of 3\n\n\n                               UNITED STATES DISTRICT COURT\n                              NORTHERN DISTRICT OF CALIFORNIA\n\n\n  YARIDA OROZCO,                                     Case No. 25-cv-08325-PHK\n\n                 Plaintiff,                          ORDER SETTING INITIAL CASE\n          v.                                         MANAGEMENT CONFERENCE\n                                                     AND ADR DEADLINES\n  TESLA, INC.,\n                 Defendant.\n\n\n       This action is assigned to the Honorable Peter H. Kang.\n       Service of documents. When serving the complaint or notice of removal, the plaintiff or\nremoving defendant must serve on all other parties a copy of this order and the supplementary\nmaterial specified in Civil Local Rule 4-2.\n         Magistrate Judge Jurisdiction. This case has been randomly assigned to a magistrate\njudge, who, with written consent of all parties, may conduct all proceedings in a case, including\nall pretrial and trial proceedings, entry of judgment and post-trial motions, with appeal directly to\nthe United States Court of Appeals for the Ninth Circuit. See \u201cConsenting to the Jurisdiction of a\nMagistrate Judge\u201d on the Court\u2019s webpage at www.cand.uscourts.gov for more information.\n        Plaintiff or the removing party must complete and file the attached form \u201cConsent or\nDeclination to Magistrate Judge Jurisdiction\u201d (also available at www.cand.uscourts.gov/forms)\nwithin 14 days of case initiation, and all other parties must do so within 14 days of appearing in\nthe case, or as otherwise ordered by the Clerk or magistrate judge.\n       Availability of Alternative Dispute Resolution. This action is assigned to the\nAlternative Dispute Resolution (ADR) Multi-Option Program governed by ADR Local Rule 3.\nCounsel and clients shall familiarize themselves with that rule and with the material entitled\n\u201cDispute Resolution Procedures in the Northern District of California\u201d on the Court\u2019s ADR\nwebpage at www.cand.uscourts.gov/adr.\n        Important case management dates. Counsel must comply with the dates listed below\nunless the judge otherwise orders.\n\f       Case 3:25-cv-08325-PHK             Document 4         Filed 10/01/25      Page 2 of 3\n\n\n\nCase Management Event                                                     Deadline\n\nFile Certification of Conflicts and Interested Entities or Persons.       Upon first appearance\n(See Civil L.R. 3-15)                                                     (supplement as necessary)\n\nDeadline to file ADR Certification.                                       12/10/2025\n(See ADR L.R. 3)\n\nDeadline to meet and confer re: initial disclosures, early settlement,    12/10/2025\nADR process selection, and discovery plan.\n(See F.R. Civ. P. 26(f))\nDeadline to make initial disclosures.                                     12/24/2025\n(See F.R. Civ. P. 26(a)(1))\n\nDeadline to file Joint Case Management Statement.                         12/24/2025\n(See Standing Order for All Judges of the Northern District of\nCalifornia)\n\nInitial Case Management Conference location: Courtroom F, 15th            12/31/2025 at 11:00 AM\nFloor, 450 Golden Gate Avenue, San Francisco, CA\n\n\n\n\n               Order Setting Initial Case Management Conference & ADR Deadlines \u2014 Page 2\n\f         Case 3:25-cv-08325-PHK          Document 4       Filed 10/01/25      Page 3 of 3\n\n\n\n                               UNITED STATES DISTRICT COURT\n\n                              NORTHERN DISTRICT OF CALIFORNIA\n\n\n\n  YARIDA OROZCO,                                    Case No. 25-cv-08325-PHK\n\n                 Plaintiff,\n                                                    CONSENT OR DECLINATION\n          v.                                        TO MAGISTRATE JUDGE\n                                                    JURISDICTION\n  TESLA, INC.,\n                 Defendant.\n\nINSTRUCTIONS: Please indicate below by checking one of the two boxes whether you (if you\nare the party) or the party you represent (if you are an attorney in the case) choose(s) to consent\nor decline to magistrate judge jurisdiction in this matter. Sign this form below your selection.\n\n       \u2610 CONSENT to Magistrate Judge Jurisdiction\n\n        In accordance with the provisions of 28 U.S.C. \u00a7 636(c), I voluntarily consent to have a\nUnited States magistrate judge conduct all further proceedings in this case, including trial and\nentry of final judgment. I understand that appeal from the judgment shall be taken directly to the\nUnited States Court of Appeals for the Ninth Circuit.\n\n       OR\n\n       \u2610 DECLINE Magistrate Judge Jurisdiction\n\n       In accordance with the provisions of 28 U.S.C. \u00a7 636(c), I decline to have a United States\nmagistrate judge conduct all further proceedings in this case and I hereby request that this case be\nreassigned to a United States district judge.\n\n\n\n DATE:                                           NAME:\n\n\n                                                                      Signature or \u201c/s/\u201d\n                                         COUNSEL FOR\n                                         (OR \u201cPRO SE\u201d):\n\f", "ocr_status": 1, "date_upload": "2025-11-27T13:45:30.871464-08:00", "document_number": "4", "attachment_number": null, "pacer_doc_id": "035026266677", "is_available": true, "is_free_on_pacer": null, "is_sealed": false, "document_type": 1, "description": "Initial Case Management Scheduling Order with ADR Deadlines", "acms_document_guid": ""}], "date_created": "2025-10-01T15:37:22.678166-07:00", "date_modified": "2025-10-01T15:37:22.736117-07:00", "date_filed": "2025-10-01", "time_filed": "15:22:40", "entry_number": 4, "recap_sequence_number": "2025-10-01.001", "pacer_sequence_number": 12, "description": "", "tags": []}, {"resource_uri": "https://www.courtlistener.com/api/rest/v4/docket-entries/439555329/", "id": 439555329, "docket": "https://www.courtlistener.com/api/rest/v4/dockets/71505605/", "recap_documents": [{"resource_uri": "https://www.courtlistener.com/api/rest/v4/recap-documents/454086184/", "id": 454086184, "tags": [], "absolute_url": "", "date_created": "2025-10-01T09:46:40.370174-07:00", "date_modified": "2025-10-01T09:46:40.435726-07:00", "sha1": "", "page_count": null, "file_size": null, "filepath_local": null, "filepath_ia": "", "ia_upload_failure_count": null, "thumbnail": null, "thumbnail_status": 0, "plain_text": "", "ocr_status": null, "date_upload": null, "document_number": "", "attachment_number": null, "pacer_doc_id": "", "is_available": false, "is_free_on_pacer": null, "is_sealed": null, "document_type": 1, "description": "~Util - Case Assigned by Intake", "acms_document_guid": ""}], "date_created": "2025-10-01T09:46:40.337647-07:00", "date_modified": "2025-10-01T09:46:40.337662-07:00", "date_filed": "2025-10-01", "time_filed": "09:12:22", "entry_number": null, "recap_sequence_number": "2025-10-01.001", "pac